I found 10 issues in `2026-09-24-swiftui-gap-closure`. I reviewed commits `b14ada40..233ef4ec` (only wave 1 has run so far) and there were no working-tree changes. `check.test.ts` passes (148 tests). I also ran the four `machine_env` detect commands directly on this machine and each printed a value: `27.0`, `iOS Simulator`, `iPhone 18 Pro`, `27.0`. I didn't include stale doc counts that unit U8 (wave 3) is already set to fix.

Findings 1 and 2 are backed by local tests. Finding 1 is the most serious: if the detect commands are run exactly as setup's instructions write them, all four fail, so setup never offers a detected default.

